                        </item>
                      </items>
                    </chunk>
                    <chunk name="param_input" index="0">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Which climate file to use. Click the widget and choose Weather file (catalog)… to pick from the catalog with a map and a spec sheet; the value stored is the file's own name (e.g. DEU_BE_Berlin-Tempelhof.AP.103840_TMYx.2009-2023). A station name, WMO id, country or dataset year still works as a search — the best match nearest the site wins — and a direct EPW or ZIP URL is downloaded as-is. A full address or place (e.g. the Site Picker's Address) that no file is named after is located on the map and the nearest file taken. Choose Open-Meteo (ERA5) — or type Open-Meteo 2019 — to build a file for the SITE (wire Latitude/Longitude, or set the Earth Anchor Point) from ERA5 reanalysis: one actual year, last year unless one is given, on the 0.25° cell. The same menu builds PVGIS (a typical year), NASA POWER (an actual year, from 2001) and ERA5 via Copernicus CDS (an actual year with measured radiation; it needs your own free CDS token, in the ECMWF_DATASTORES_KEY environment variable or ~/.cdsapirc, and the dataset licence accepted on the CDS website) and NSRDB (GOES TMY, a typical year, or GOES aggregated, an actual year from 1998, both PSM v4 on a 4 km cell over the western hemisphere; a release of Eddy3D ships a shared NLR API key for it, which your own (a free key from developer.nlr.gov, with your name and email) replaces: NSRDB_API_KEY, NSRDB_FULL_NAME and NSRDB_EMAIL, or ~/.nsrdbrc). Credits: weather data by Open-Meteo.com (CC BY 4.0); PVGIS, European Commission Joint Research Centre; NASA Langley POWER Project; Copernicus Climate Change Service (ERA5); National Solar Radiation Database (NLR). Terms: THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">e8ac1ee1-7d4b-461d-bac4-e26cc46d2484</item>
                        <item name="Multiple" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Station</item>
                        <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Station</item>
                        <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                        <item name="Options" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">OneBuilding (nearest TMYx)
EnergyPlus (nearest)
Open-Meteo (ERA5)
Open-Meteo (IFS 9 km)
Open-Meteo (CERRA 5 km)
Open-Meteo (ICON-D2 2 km)
Open-Meteo (HRRR 3 km)
Open-Meteo (ERA5 + satellite radiation)
PVGIS (typical year)
NASA POWER (MERRA-2 + CERES)
ERA5 via Copernicus CDS
NSRDB (GOES TMY, PSM v4)
NSRDB (GOES aggregated, PSM v4)</item>
                        <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                        <item name="Value" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">OneBuilding (nearest TMYx)</item>
