                    <chunk name="param_input" index="5">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">How many processes the Radiance chain spreads its sensors over.
Auto (default) decides from the chain. With Fast Matrices on (the default) the sun term is finished on the host and the container's multiplies are binary and quick, so Auto stays at ONE process: measured at 4,500 and 14,600 sensors, splitting changed the run time by less than its run-to-run noise. With Fast Matrices off (the ASCII chain), or with tree crowns (their sun multiply stays in the container), the annual multiplies (dctimestep + rmtxop) are most of the run at thousands of sensors and neither program has a threading flag, so Auto splits the sensors over up to the machine's physical cores minus two, never below 500 sensors a block — 4,500 ASCII sensors took 220 s in one process and 117 s in nine.
Off is always one process; 2, 4, 8 or 16 processes are honoured as given, which is also the way to cap a shared machine.
This never changes the answer: every sensor is traced by identical commands against identical octrees and sky matrices; only which file it was listed in differs.
Only applies when Radiance Reflections is on.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">67000687-e783-4094-acfc-b574c36ed69f</item>
                        <item name="Multiple" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Parallelize</item>
                        <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Parallelize</item>
                        <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                        <item name="Options" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Auto
Off (single process)
2 processes
4 processes
8 processes
16 processes</item>
                        <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                        <item name="Value" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Auto</item>
                      </items>
                      <chunks count="2">
                        <chunk name="Attributes">
