                    <chunk name="param_input" index="6">
                      <items count="7">
                        <item name="Access" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">1</item>
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Optional hours of the year (1-8760, e.g. from the HOY component) the study is about. EnergyPlus then simulates only the days spanning them, plus 3 lead-in days, instead of the whole year — its cost is close to linear in simulated hours, so a heat-wave week runs many times faster.
The MRT result is still 8760 hours: outside the period the surrounding surfaces are assumed to sit at air temperature, exactly as with EnergyPlus Surfaces off, so read results only for the hours given here. A selection that wraps the new year runs (nearly) the whole year. Empty (default) = full year.
Only applies when EnergyPlus Surfaces is on. The Radiance chain works on annual sky matrices and is not shortened by this.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">de6e241c-aac7-4431-af27-7b02f2a22713</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Run Period</item>
                        <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Run Period</item>
                        <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                        <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                      </items>
                      <chunks count="1">
                        <chunk name="Attributes">
                          <items count="2">
                            <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                              <X>2739</X>
                              <Y>1595</Y>
                              <W>107</W>
                              <H>20</H>
                            </item>
                            <item name="Pivot" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                              <X>2794</X>
                              <Y>1605</Y>
                            </item>
                          </items>
                        </chunk>
                      </chunks>
                    </chunk>
                    <chunk name="param_input" index="7">
                      <items count="6">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">true (default): the Radiance chain moves its annual matrices as binary files and the sun term is finished as a sparse product on the host — several times quicker on large sensor grids, a quarter of the disk, and free of the three-digit rounding ASCII sky matrices carry (up to 0.5 % of the beam in an hour).
false: the ASCII chain Eddy3D shipped before this input existed, kept as the control and the way back. For Two-Phase DDS the two agree to float rounding apart from that rounding. Two-Phase (preview) reads its beam straight from the sampled ray-traced coefficients, which the ASCII chain does not reproduce from run to run (about 0.7 % of the annual total, and more in single hours); the binary chain does.
Only applies when Radiance Reflections is on.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">cad4be10-f349-460f-8917-6fea5e1c0537</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Fast Matrices</item>
