                    <chunk name="param_input" index="10">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">How EnergyPlus exchanges longwave between the inside faces of the thermal model.
CarrollMRT (default): a mean-radiant-temperature network, linear in the number of surfaces.
ScriptF: EnergyPlus's own default and what Eddy3D ran before this input existed — an exact exchange that inverts a surfaces x surfaces matrix before the first timestep. Fine for a few hundred surfaces; at 6,655 it is about 80 minutes during which EnergyPlus prints nothing.
Outside surface temperatures between the two stayed within 0.2 K (0.01 K on average) on the case this was measured on.
Only applies when EnergyPlus Surfaces is on.</item>
